First, I should think of tasks that require local processing. For example, image recognition in real time without internet. Then, maybe something like voice assistants that can understand and respond instantly. Also, local data processing could include things like location-based services without needing to send data to the cloud.

Next, real-time processing is another area. On-device AI can handle tasks like translating speech in real time, which a cloud model might not be able to do efficiently. Then, there's personalization with local data, like a phone's AI adjusting settings based on user behavior without cloud data.

